  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why the hook reads from both",
      "items": [
        "Health Connect holds aggregated history written by any app, so it answers what the day totalled, not what the sensor says now",
        "The HAL feed is zero latency and unaggregated, which is the only way to show a step or heart rate reading as it happens",
        "hasStepCounter and hasHeartRateSensor report the live side separately, because a device can have the store without the sensor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What the user controls",
      "items": [
        "Health data sits behind individual permissions such as READ_STEPS and READ_HEART_RATE, not one blanket grant",
        "The system privacy dashboard lets a user audit and revoke access per app, so a granted permission is not permanent",
        "sdkStatus reports whether Health Connect is present and usable, so an unavailable store is a state rather than a thrown error"
      ]
    }
  ]
